        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0342" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg336"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 3 of the 25th
                    ultimo, informing me that the majority report of the committee on the bill in
                    the Hawaiian Legislature to convene delegates to frame a new constitution is
                    opposed to such a convention, and stating, also, that His Majesty is believed to
                    be now opposed to such a convention.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
